f they were  broke  pop culture went to a strange place in  the late 90s in music the decade started  with nirvana  and somehow ended with the all-singing  all-dancing backstreet boys releasing  the top-selling album of 1999  meanwhile film enjoyed a much more  consistent 10 years but if there was a  strange trend in cinema and television  during the 90s it was media that fell  within the vaguely defined teen genre  while buffy transcends the 90s teen  explosion the same can't be said i know  what you did last summer or cruel  intentions  two significant works of the era and  genre both prominently featuring geller  she wasn't exactly typecast but her  persona became very closely tied to a  distinct point in time and a distinct  entertainment demographic  trends go out of style and become retro  cool again in cycles  but casting geller in a 2020 film or tv  show might be kind of like commissioning  dave roll to make a soundcloud rap album  you know he can do it and he might even  do an exceptional job but it just feels  strange keller looked like she was on  her way back to the top of the  television heap as recently as 2013.  on paper the small screen return of  robin williams looked like a no fail  situation  thus launched cbs's the crazy ones on  which geller played the daughter of  william's eccentric advertising  executive  i think that's the thing that people  don't realize is you think he's this  crazy funny  mrs doubtfire or aladdin genie and he's  just the kindest  like most gentle man alas the show only  completed its first 22 episode season  before the network pulled the plug  cancellation after only one season isn't  a meaningful indicator of a television  show's quality  and on the flip side bad shows sometimes  stay on tv for years  the crazy ones was also doomed by  outside circumstance  williams passed away in 2014 a few  months after the final episode of the  crazy ones aired  so even if the first season had been a  bigger success a second season might  have been impossible without a  significant recasting or possibly a  reconfiguration of the entire show  nevertheless the crazy ones didn't  become a lasting hit  geller has a number of projects  percolating at various stages of  development one particular production is  of unique interest to a base of hardcore  fans  here's a hint it's a project based on a  cartoon in which the character geller  portrays fights a skeleton bad guy  voiced by the one and only mark hamill  announced in 2019 netflix's animated  masters of the universe revelation  features geller lending her voice  alongside a star-studded cast  this isn't the only modern masters of  the universe project but it's a whole  lot less murky than the much delayed  movie this isn't geller's first time  working as a voice actor  she also appeared as april in 2007's  tmnt  and has popped up frequently on star  wars rebels and robot chicken  oddly enough she did not provide the  voice of buffy summers in the unaired  pilot of 2004's buffy the vampire slayer  the animated series  if you're the sort of person who can't  be bothered with the media unless it's  related to superheroes space aliens or  some variety of supernatural forces then  it's understandable if you think geller  fell off the face of the planet after  buffy ended in 2003  if you don't tune in to daytime talk  shows or read celebrity gossip magazines  you might have thought she's been  missing all these years  geller is still famous enough for daily  mail photographers to follow her around  while she does normal stuff like go  grocery shopping and pick up the mail  meanwhile the folks at people magazine  think geller and prince adopting puppies  is a newsworthy event  which granted it is but mostly because  every puppy is newsworthy as recently as  october of 2020 geller went on the kelly  clarkson show and announced that her  children are finally old enough to watch  buffy and they binged the heck out of it  to help make the best of the cobit 19  lockdown  she explained i didn't know if they'd be  into it but they are so into it  except i'm the world's biggest  disappointment for them because they'll  always ask questions and i'll be like  i don't remember i'll have to text  someone and ask i think they know it  better than i do at this point  to be fair who really remembers what  happened at their jobs 20 years ago  but my son actually thinks that i'm cool  now  cookies brownies cakes donuts a lot of  the time they're loaded with excess  sugar salt and chemicals we can't  pronounce  the problem is they're also delicious a  few years back geller ran up against  this age-old conundrum  and decided to do something about it in  a 2019 interview she told aol  our kids were really interested in  baking and my knowledge of baking was  all eating and i don't have the time to  get 30 million ingredients  so i went to the store and we were  shocked that in 2015 the only things  were the traditional legacy boxed brands  where the number one ingredient was salt  the lack of baking mix that wasn't  aggressively terrible for human health  prompted geller to co-found what she and  her business associates call the junk  free baking company foodstirs  and if the photos on the boxes are any  indication food stores make some  delicious treats  we just started really baking together  and having these like really fun moments  and there's nothing a kid loves more  than  dough and rolling it and making a mess  in the kitchen foodstirs is also unique  as a professional endeavor geller's  undergone that has nothing to do with  buffy or movies or anything which we as  the content consuming public would  normally associate with her  as it turns out people do have lives  outside of their television personas  geller is a deeply committed mom like so  many mothers around the world but the  key difference here is that typical moms  only end up in the news if they do  something horrible or amazing  keller parents just as hard as anyone  while also being the kind of famous  person who is photographed when she runs  out to the store for milk  raising little ones takes up a whole lot  of time and attention since keller and  prince officially became parents in 2009  child rearing has likely eaten into time  both of them could have otherwise  devoted to acting in r-rated films  screaming cuss words and loudly joking  about adult topics around the house  granted most of those things don't seem  to be of interest to the pair but it's  definitely clear that their kids take up  a major amount of space in their lives  in recent years geller has cultivated a  mutually beneficial relationship  between her media persona and her mom  hood most notably her business venture  with foodstirs was partially inspired by  a family treat-baking activity  she's also indicated taking a hands-on  approach to her son's coveted mandated  zoom learning situation and at least two  unrelated interviews  all evidence indicates that geller  spends loads of time with her offspring  and that's just the way she likes it  geller does quite a bit of partnering  with specific brands like many  celebrities  thus it would be inaccurate to describe  her work in optical health as charity  however even if she's advertising  products she goes about it in a way that  encourages people to make sure their  eyes are in tip-top shape  and hey it's much better to be a  spokesperson for vision than cigarettes  or cheap vodka  according to the daily mail geller was  on an australian trip to promote an  optical retail chain when she told a  crowd of fans  i was working on buffy and getting  horrible headaches and squinting the  doctor on set told me to get my eyes  checked  i had no health insurance so i had never  had my eyes checked  he told me i was blind as a bat more  recently geller's recentered her optical  related endeavors on childhood myopia  apparently fixating on screens all day  is pretty unhealthy for developing  eyeballs  who would 